invariant: INV-16
file: src/aead_avx512.c
catches: aead_avx512_equiv_test
reason: each pass of the AVX-512 seal absorbs the ciphertext of its own pass in
  place of the pass before it, so it reads bytes it has not yet encrypted
  and the tag is wrong for every seal of AEAD_AVX512_MIN bytes or more.
  bin/aead_avx512_equiv_test runs the seal's own text over the lane models
  on every machine and compares its tag with the two-pass AEAD's.

--- old
        const uint8_t *hash = ct + offset - PASS_BYTES;
--- new
        const uint8_t *hash = ct + offset;
